        </introduction>

        <task>
            <statement>
                <p>
                    Sketch a scatterplot comparing the baseline biomarker level to the week-12 biomarker level in the control group in the axes below.
                </p>
                <image source="images/blankQ1axes.jpg" width="50%">
                    <shortdescription>A blank set of positive axes.</shortdescription>
                </image>
            </statement>
        </task>

        <task>
            <statement>
                <p>
                    Sketch a scatterplot comparing the baseline biomarker level to the week-12 biomarker level in the treatment group in the sane set of axes above.
                </p>
            </statement>
        </task>

        <task workspace="2in">
            <statement>
                <p>
                    Compute the regression line for each set of data. Then, sketch them onto the image above using the same color scheme you used previously. For example, if you sketched the control group in red, its regression line should be red as well. 
                </p>
            </statement>
        </task>

        <task workspace="0.5in">
            <statement>
                <p>
                    Compare and contrast the relationships. Which appears to be a better fit and why? 
                </p>
            </statement>
        </task>
